Usage: unexpand [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Convert spaces to tabs.

Convert spaces to tabs. By default, only convert leading spaces to tabs.
Use -a to convert all spaces.

Supports GNU tab lists, including /N and +N repeat tab stops.

OPTIONS:
  -t, --tabs ARG    specify tab stop positions (default: 8)
  -a, --all         convert all spaces, not just leading ones
  -f, --first-only  convert only leading sequences of blanks
  -U, --no-utf8     interpret input file as 8-bit ASCII rather than UTF-8
  -NUM              same as --tabs=NUM
      --help        display this help and exit
  -V, --version     output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
